    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests how {@link StringSubstitutor} handles escaped variable prefixes. <p>The default escape character is {@code $}. A doubled {@code $$} collapses to a single literal {@code $}, so a template that starts with three dollar signs ({@code $$$}) ends up with two ({@code $$}) in the result. This is the \"3 to 2\" escaping case under test.</p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
